# A mid-stream disconnect_after cut (testdata/faux/behaviour-retry.yaml
# style) followed by a normal follow-up step: the cut retries and the
# reconnected continuation lands as its own text.
# The retry backoff is fixed at ten minutes, so the cut partial text and
# the countdown stay on screen until the scenario presses r (retry now).
@faux testdata/faux/qa/errors-stream-cut-midtext.yaml
@env HARNESS_RETRY_DELAY_MS=600000

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE tell me something long
SHOT typed
KEY enter
# Once the retry lands, kiln replaces the cut partial text with the fresh
# reply, so the partial is checked while the countdown holds it on screen.
WAITFOR /Here is the first half[\s\S]*Retrying in \d+s · attempt 2 of 4/ 20
EXPECT /Here is the first half/
SHOT cut-point
KEY r
WAITFOR /Reconnected on attempt 2/ 20
SHOT reconnected
WAITFOR /reconnected continuation lands here/ 20
EXPECT /reconnected continuation lands here, safe and sound/
SHOT continuation
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
